B.Pf=A.a(s(["A) Children who have developed a regular reading habit generally acquire a broader vocabulary and stronger empathy skills.","B) Unless children read regularly, they can never communicate effectively with peers.","C) Although reading regularly expands vocabulary, it rarely contributes to empathy in children.","D) Regular reading habits were first encouraged in European schools to improve vocabulary.","E) Having stronger empathy skills forces children to read academic books more regularly."]),t.s)
B.Sc=new A.dl(B.dU,null,null,'TR \u2192 EN: "D\xfczenli okuma al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 edinmi\u015f \xe7ocuklar genellikle daha geni\u015f bir kelime da\u011farc\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve daha g\xfc\xe7l\xfc empati becerileri geli\u015ftirir."',B.Pf,0,'\xd6zne ("D\xfczenli okuma al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 edinmi\u015f \xe7ocuklar") + zarf ("generally") + y\xfcklem ("acquire a broader vocabulary and stronger empathy skills") \u2192 A \u015f\u0131kk\u0131 tam e\u015fle\u015fir.','Relative Clause \xf6znesini ("Children who...") ve "generally" zarf\u0131n\u0131 yakala!')
B.MI=A.a(s(["A) To argue that trees compete violently and never share nutrients","B) To explain how underground fungal networks allow forest trees to exchange nutrients and warning signals","C) To describe methods for eliminating beetles from commercial timber farms","D) To prove that shaded saplings require more sunlight than canopy trees","E) To compare phosphorus levels in tropical and boreal soils"]),t.s)
